# TYPE - Display a text file

```text
TYPE [DU:]filename [/P]
```

## Read a file

TYPE sends text to the console. Add /P to pause during a long listing.
Ctrl-C stops the display and returns to the command prompt.

```text
TYPE A0:README.TXT /P
```

## Browse pages

A leading colon selects TYPE.COM. Its paged viewer can go back to an
earlier page as well as advance.

```text
:TYPE A0:README.TXT /P
```

For a file containing binary data, use [DUMP](DUMP.HLP) to see the
stored bytes and their offsets.
